  "limits": "The unchanged gateway/primary recovery regression now passes, together with new/invalid export retries, bounded WebSocket 401 handling, ordinary external-auth control and the full 144-test provider library on 1e3e2c47ea. Three stronger controls on 5119f29178 execute real managers, actual export processes and real catalog/inference HTTP requests: equivalent providers share one upstream export, source changes and unrelated owners separate caches, old-source/old-token rejections cannot clear newer or identical-byte generations, mixed owners refuse before another command, and an aborted caller retains its actual manager until the blocked command finishes. These are local manager/source and process controls, not native credential-image proof, complete feature contracts, Windows/Linux behavior or a full native gate at the changed source."
